==Pre-match==
===Ticketing===
The international ticket sales phase for the general public ran from 5 to 27 June 2014. Tickets were available in three price categories: [[Pound sterling|£]]110, £75, and £40.<ref>{{cite news |title=UEFA Super Cup Cardiff 2014 tickets on sale |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0250-0c51058f6115-0fd36e826c2b-1000--uefa-super-cup-cardiff-2014-tickets-on-sale/ |website=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=5 June 2014 }}</ref>

===Officials===
England's [[Mark Clattenburg]] was appointed by UEFA as the referee of the match, accompanied by an all-English team of officials: assistant referees Simon Beck and Stuart Burt, fourth official [[Darren England]], and additional assistant referees [[Michael Oliver (referee)|Michael Oliver]] and [[Anthony Taylor (referee)|Anthony Taylor]].<ref name="officials">{{cite news |title=Clattenburg to referee UEFA Super Cup |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0250-0c5104e256a7-e116d816fcf5-1000--clattenburg-to-referee-uefa-super-cup/ |website=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=30 July 2014 }}</ref>

The match was the first in a UEFA club competition to use [[vanishing spray]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Vanishing spray paint approved for UEFA games |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0253-0d7fdd76e9aa-30a128a937cd-1000--vanishing-spray-paint-approved-for-uefa-games/ |website=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=8 August 2014 }}</ref>

{{clear}}

==Match==

===Team selection===
Real Madrid midfielder [[Xabi Alonso]] was suspended for the match, due to breaches of conduct in the Champions League Final, for which he was also suspended.<ref>{{cite news |title=Alonso one-match ban confirmed for Super Cup |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0250-0c510575e48c-103297d3e36a-1000--alonso-one-match-ban-confirmed-for-super-cup/ |website=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=8 August 2014 }}</ref>

New signings [[Toni Kroos]] and [[James Rodríguez]] made their competitive debuts for Real Madrid; another new signing, [[Keylor Navas]], was an unused substitute. Sevilla gave competitive debuts to [[Denis Suárez]], [[Aleix Vidal]] and [[Grzegorz Krychowiak]], as well as substitute [[Iago Aspas]]. [[Nicolás Pareja]] and [[Daniel Carriço]] represented Sevilla for the first time since their loans were made permanent.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/european/11029877/Real-Madrid-2-Sevilla-0-Cristiano-Ronaldo-at-the-double-as-European-Cup-winners-claim-Uefa-Super-Cup-in-Cardiff.html |title=Real Madrid 2 Sevilla 0: Cristiano Ronaldo at the double as European Cup winners claim Uefa Super Cup in Cardiff |date=12 August 2014 |work=Daily Telegraph |access-date=19 August 2014 }}</ref>

